## AI Readiness Analysis

AI Readiness analysis evaluates how clearly a website can be interpreted by artificial intelligence systems.

The analysis focuses on several factors, including:

- clarity of business description
- semantic structure of the website
- structured data implementation
- consistency of company information
- trust signals such as legal pages and policies
- for organisation-controlled conversational systems: approved sources, high-risk claim controls, grounding, output guardrails, testing, traceability and human escalation

The goal is to assess whether public evidence makes the identity, services, context, permissions and action boundaries of a website consistently understandable. Results describe observable readiness signals and do not guarantee a specific AI-system outcome. Where a company operates a chatbot or agent, the analysis can activate the AI Output & Liability Readiness module and separately assess whether the system can correctly answer before it is allowed to act.
